## Permissions

```
d rwx r-x r-x
| |   |   |
| |   |   +-- others
| |   +------ group
| +---------- owner
+------------ type (d = directory, - = file, l = symlink)
```
Always 10 characters. `r` read, `w` write, `x` execute, `-` none. On a directory, `x` means can enter it with `cd`.

**Number mode:** r = 4, w = 2, x = 1, added per group.

| Digit | Permission |
|-------|-----------|
| 7 | rwx |
| 6 | rw- |
| 5 | r-x |
| 4 | r-- |
| 0 | --- |

`rwxr-xr-x` = 7 5 5 = `755`

```bash
ls -ld folder
```
Permissions of the folder itself, not its contents.

```bash
chmod 755 folder
```
Sets permissions using numbers.

Common modes: `755` folders/scripts, `644` normal files, `700` private folder (`~/.ssh`), `600` private file (SSH key).

