## ls -S (sort by size)

```bash
ls -s
```
Shows allocated space (blocks) at the start of each line.

```bash
ls -ls
```
Long format + allocated space.

```bash
ls -lS
```
Sort by size, largest first.

```bash
ls -lh
```
Human-readable sizes: `4.0K`, `1.2M`, `3.4G`. 1K = 1024 bytes.

```bash
ls -l --si
```
Same but 1K = 1000 bytes. Rarely used.

```bash
ls -lhS
```
Everyday form: biggest first, readable sizes.

